    "last_updated": "2026-06-17",
    "v5_baseline": "Dasher v5 shipped native frontends for Windows, Linux/GTK, macOS and iOS (Android was a separate project; Mac/iPhone were unmaintained by the 5.0 beta). Input covered mouse, stylus/tablet, touch, multitouch, tilt, joystick (Linux) and socket input (the conduit for eye/gaze trackers). Notable v5 features: game/training mode, eye-tracker autocalibration, PPM family language models, Kanji/Pinyin conversion, and three TTS backends (SAPI / speech-dispatcher / flite).",
